    "created_at": "2020-02-11T20:46:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-02-11T20:46:37Z",
    "body": "Perhaps it's not difficult for some developers but I guess I need to cross-compile every dependencies into static libs (like *.a not *.so files), Yes I could just do that or maybe just download a [zsh-static binary](https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/bionic/arm64/zsh-static/5.4.2-3ubuntu3.1).\r\n\r\nDealing with static binaries is the last thing I want to do, and all these library-linking and cross-compiling are also painful jobs for most developers. That's one of the reasons that I became a Go/Rust developer. (I don't want to turn this thread into a [PL](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Programming_language) level so let's stop it right here.)\r\n\r\nThe first line I saw on readme is \r\n\r\n> Starship is the minimal, blazing fast, and extremely customizable prompt for any shell!\r\n\r\nI knew ash is probably a minor shell, but I believe there are a lot people using it for some reasons, so why not push it to the limit!",
