    "created_at": "2022-06-27T18:30:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-06-27T18:30:45Z",
    "body": "My guess is that there's not a way to make a vast majority of starship features work with any variants of the almquist shell. For example, command duration is almost certainly not going to work, keymaps and pipestatuses are out of the question, and I can't find a way to get it to report background jobs).\r\n\r\nHowever, if you're okay with a bunch of the shell-linked functionality being broken, the following works for me under dash on Arch (I can't find a pre-built version of `ash` right now, so YMMV):\r\n\r\n`PS1='$(starship prompt --status \"$?\" --path \"$PWD\")'`\r\n\r\n* * *\r\n\r\nI'm not opposed to merging general support, but someone would need to go through and figure out which features can be made to work, which features don't, put all the appropriate things in the documentation, and then open a PR.\r\n\r\nIt's not even clear to me whether an eval variant like we see for other shells would be worth it: those are usually used to set up more complex functionality using shell-specific features like functions, hooks, traps, signal handling, etc, but it seems ash just doesn't have any of these. So there's nothing for an eval-init to do.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
